"body": "## Problem\nThe real Moltbook /home response and current skill example omit your_direct_messages, while exposing an explicit public unread_notification_count. The old bridge refused before reservation, so no post was created.\n\n## Change\nSupport both documented response shapes. Current responses require a nonnegative integer public notification count; legacy/present DM sections retain strict counter validation. Unread public activity and reported DMs still block new posts. Missing, malformed, Boolean, negative or string counters refuse before any write.\n\nUnreported DM visibility is explicitly retained in summaries, operation results and durable receipt context. It is never fabricated as an empty inbox. Identity, budgets, origin restrictions, duplicate guards and content verification are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\nAll 91 bridge cases pass. A real read-only home call returns zero public obligations with direct_message_visibility=not_reported. No raw POST fallback or fake publication was used.",
